From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bsp2020 <bsp2020@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 02:28:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 32/36] moe cache: KV segment -- lent KV rows as an
 expert-cache tier below the arena

GGML_MOE_KV_LEND=1 + GGML_MOE_KV_SEG=1 (default off; unset GGML_MOE_KV_SEG = off).
Under -sm tensor every device lends the rows of its own K/V slices past the
context in use (ggml_backend_meta_tensor_simple; GGML_MOE_KV_LEND_META=0 off,
=1 device 0 only).  Each table that seeds gets an equal share of its device's
lent slots, filled after its decode policy with its next-hottest non-resident
experts (heat rank) and then by demand (a cold miss with ghost >= 2 takes a free
slot or replaces the share's least recently used copy), copied from the RAM
tier with cold_ptrs[e] written in the same fill job.  The copy serves the cold
read; the arena policy sees the same miss as without the segment and an
admission fills from the copy, so the arena evolves as without it
(GGML_MOE_KV_SEG_TIER=0: copies count as hits and are never admitted).
Take-backs (moe_cache_kv_need) flush the fill batch, synchronise, point the
copies back at RAM and zero the rows.  GGML_MOE_PF_LEND defaults off with the
segment.  Also carried from the parked lending / borrowing work: per-device
lending with batched pointer scatter on take-back (direct write when the
device lookup fails), fill-batch jobs that read a queued fill's slot flush
first, GGML_MOE_KV_BORROW (default off).

Fable design + logic reviews (no open must-fix).  Production config,
-c 262144, two rounds (FINDINGS 935): decode +2.5 % at 4.2k, +1.7..2.5 % at
101k, midpf +1.4..2.5 %; prefill equal except -0.6 % on a 260k prompt
(stepwise take-backs); output identical.
