+// KV borrowing (GGML_MOE_KV_BORROW=1, needs GGML_MOE_KV_LEND=1; default off): a decode miss served cold, whose expert
+// has no copy in a KV slot yet, is copied there from its RAM copy, and cold_ptrs[e] names the copy (one batched
+// job: the pointer write and the copy are one kernel, ahead of this layer's readers on the decode stream).  So the
+// lent KV rows hold the experts decode actually misses, not only what the arena evicted: extra cache capacity that
+// the KV takes back as the context grows (moe_cache_kv_need; the copy is a duplicate, dropping it is a pointer write).
+// GGML_MOE_KV_BORROW_TOUCH (default 2): the cold touches an expert needs since it was last resident before it is
